 Complete Phase 1 code review, source/runtime identities, original failures and resolved findings, actual checks/QC, milestone TODO aggregation and exit assessment are in the [phase report](reports/phases/1/PHASE-REPORT.md). Scoped runtime assistance added explicit `-B` only to existing Python child argv in tests/checker; no semantic or governing amendment. After correcting the consumer quoting defect, 23 unit/18 integration tests, 36 isolated extracted module cases and every runnable user-guide fence pass on Python 3.12.14 with bytecode disabled. Initial failed runs remain retained. T-001–T-008 closing commits individually contain one initial owning checkbox plus result/evidence. Current fork tracking is explicitly disabled; copied hosted identities are protected and no issue/milestone write is made.
 
 This concrete T-009 report/checklist/result candidate awaits coordinator acceptance before the owning commit, immediate trial phase publication/readback, and two-parent local main integration/merged checks/trial main publication. Status in the proposed candidate reflects verified task and parent exits; durable completion and integration are not asserted before their actual operations. Phase 2 is eligible only afterward for selected T-010; T-011 onward and Phase 2 main integration are outside scope.
+
+## T-010 completion evidence
+
+Selected T-009 through T-010 inclusive. Phase 1 task `dfcd658828d8e326c713683f3cdb9be05e044849` was accepted, committed and immediately published/read back to the authorized trial phase ref. Concrete report acceptance decision `c837cd750ad7bcb932add989644e8c851ce15f34` and actual merge acceptance decision `d244a40538aac6eb374fb1fd5a1a6bc76d66adce` preceded their corresponding operations. Complete Phase 1 two-parent integration `a7285d78a7fb1ee3966850656de6594317d5125f` has ordered parents `88a5c4b4424f4bba76940e40b1d6523b1f6fe191` / `dfcd658828d8e326c713683f3cdb9be05e044849`, tree `93756800aafe8abb0d8719176a14eb81ba42b4e1`. Fresh merged-state 23 unit/18 integration and 36 extracted checks passed before its immediate authorized trial main publication/readback and independent confirmation. Phase 2 activation followed that confirmation on `phase/2-json-and-stdin` from this published merge. Current fork tracking is explicitly disabled; no historical hosted object is written.
+
+Added named-file `--json` as a parser/output policy over the same completed statistics. Output has exactly integer `lines` and `words`, one object and a final newline; default exact text, BOM policy, whole-input API and error categories remain unchanged. Help, README, CLI/public module reference and root orientation describe the delivered checkpoint. No new acquisition path, public export, range or stdin capability.
+
+Meaningful test-first RED: `python -B -m unittest tests.unit.test_cli.CliTests.test_json_success_composes_with_bom_and_option_order tests.unit.test_cli.CliTests.test_json_input_failures_retain_empty_stdout_and_status tests.integration.test_cli.ModuleCliTests.test_json_semantic_matrix_and_option_composition tests.integration.test_cli.ModuleCliTests.test_json_errors_retain_status_streams_and_diagnostics tests.integration.test_cli.ModuleCliTests.test_json_option_like_filename_after_double_dash -v` ran 5 tests with 83 failing subcases because `--json` was unsupported (usage status 2). Original raw failure retained before production change. GREEN `python -B tools/check_tests.py` passes 26 unit and 21 integration tests, no skips, on Python 3.12.14 with PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 and explicit child `-B`. Coverage: fourteen independent whole-input semantic/BOM cases across five option arrangements; parsed exact keys and actual int types, final newline, API/equal exact text counts and unchanged bytes; controlled unreadability/read/decode and real missing/bad-byte JSON failures; usage validation before acquisition, rejected abbreviation, double-dash option-like filename and help.
+
+Every seven README and one public-guide runnable fence executed successfully in a private copy of current ordinary product files, avoiding uncertain root sample ownership. JSON examples produce three/five and retained BOM-only one/one objects; retained API/text/BOM/help/dash examples pass. Documented independent suite discovery also passes 26/21. Existing archive/checker and separate extracted text example pass 36 retained module cases; dedicated extracted-source JSON acceptance remains T-011, unselected and unclaimed. Documentation local links and changed whitespace pass. Review inspected minimal CLI data flow and unchanged error/acquisition/counting boundaries; no blocker found.
+
+Only T-010 initially closes in this result/evidence/tests/docs/checklist candidate. Phase 2 and milestone 2.1 remain unchecked. Publish/read back this task only to `refs/heads/trial/037-a014-cross-json` and stop on its retained phase branch; do not integrate Phase 2 into main or execute T-011 onward. Uncertain untracked root README samples are preserved and excluded from staging/archive; shared filesystem isolation cannot be certified. Other runtimes/platforms, stdin/ranges and release publication remain outside this checkpoint.
